        }
      ],
      "why": "pipelined gives 1 result/cycle, so at Fmax >= 32 MHz it clears the 32 Msps throughput constraint with margin. The 0.5 us batch deadline is the real gate: 32 back-to-back results need 32 cycles, so Fmax must be >= 64 MHz, which forces a short critical path (small n_iter, small angle_guard). Accuracy needs max_abs_err <= 2^-12, which pins data_width/n_iter/angle_guard/frac_guard/rounding to a narrow feasible band. I focus the densest budget here because it is the only family that can plausibly satisfy both the throughput and the tight batch-latency bound, and its area/accuracy trade-off is the core of the front."
    },
    {
      "budget_share": 0.45,
      "family": "pipelined_m",
      "ranges": [
        {
          "choices": [
            "trunc",
            "round"
          ],
          "high": 2,
          "low": -2,
          "param": "angle_guard"
        },
        {
